P5 deletion detector, stage B — THE PRECISION RULE, one test per condition
  ok  lexicalText strips the silence-hallucination vocabulary whisper emits over dead air
  ok  informativeWords counts a laugh once and drops it — the loudest false positive in the corpus
  ok  all five conditions satisfied -> DELETED, with the recovered words carried for the alarm
  ok  condition 2 — a decode of only fillers is NOT-SPEECH, whatever its raw word count
  ok  condition 3 — near-silence with a fabricated "Thank you." over it is NOT a deletion
  ok  condition 3 is CHANNEL-RELATIVE — the same dBFS passes on a quieter channel
  ok  condition 4 — a decode that changes with the padding is a property of the window, not the audio
  ok  condition 5a — words already in the surrounding transcript are MISTIMED, not missing
  ok  condition 5b — one inserted word must not defeat the echo test (the measured near-miss)
  ok  echoLength wants a CONTIGUOUS run; echoRatio tolerates insertions
  ok  no probe -> UNPROBED, and an unprobed span is never a deletion

P5 deletion detector — the report, and the two answers it must never conflate
  ok  guardDeletions reports a deletion with the span, the level and the recovered words
  ok  NO BURST GRID is "never looked", not "nothing found" — probeAvailable says so per channel
  ok  NO PROBE -> every candidate is unprobed and NOTHING is called a deletion
  ok  the probe budget is a HARD CAP: longest spans first, the rest reported UNPROBED
  ok  deletionWarnings names the span in clock time, quotes what is missing, and says detect-only
  ok  deletionWarnings never lets an UNADJUDICATED span read as a clean transcript
  ok  SILENCE vs DELETION side by side: silent on the silence, loud on the clause beside it

P5 word-density instrument, stage A — THE BUDGET: how much speech, how many words
  ok  tileWindows groups consecutive bursts until the window holds windowSpeechSec of speech
  ok  the shipped window is 4 s of speech — swept, and the value is what the sweep chose
  ok  a window whose bursts are too far apart is ABANDONED, never judged on a denominator of silence
  ok  a window at ordinary conversational density is NOT a candidate
  ok  THE WHOLE CLASS IN ONE ASSERTION: a window whose speech became four words IS a candidate
  ok  a WORDLESS window is never a candidate here — that is the deletion detector's class
  ok  on a channel at conversational pace the relative half is INERT — the absolute floor binds
  ok  THE COST OF THAT PROTECTION, asserted rather than hidden: a slow channel must collapse further
  ok  a confirmed DELETION is excluded from the budget — the exclusion can only remove findings
  ok  the whole channel being thin is a finding of its own, which no per-window comparison can see
  ok  the two counts a findings list cannot give: thin windows, and the ones that are 3.7's
  ok  analyzedSpeechSec is reported against burstSeconds, so "0 findings" can never read as "all clear"

P5 word-density instrument, stage B — THE PRECISION RULE, one test per condition
  ok  all six conditions satisfied -> UNDER-TRANSCRIBED, carrying what the audio returned
  ok  condition 4 — a thin window at near-silence level is NOT speech, so its budget was never real
  ok  condition 5 — A SLOW, EMPHATIC DELIVERY IS NOT A DEFECT: the audio agrees with the transcript
  ok  condition 5 — laughter cannot manufacture a recovery: eight "words", two of them informative
  ok  condition 5 — a recovery that does not survive repadding is a property of the window
  ok  condition 6 — words already in the transcript beside the window are PRESENT, not missing
  ok  condition 6 — a three-word coincidence is NOT an echo, and that is why this floor is four
  ok  no probe -> UNPROBED, and an unprobed window is never a finding

P5 word-density instrument — the report, and what it refuses to claim
